                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Made with the Unity engine by a single developer from Russia (I think, everything's in Russian in-game and you can toggle English only), this game fits perfectly in those free to play things you can find on the Google Play store (sorry Apple users, I'm poor and I own a humble Samsung phone xD) that basically go like this - you are bored, you install some games on your SD card, you play randomly through them and you uninstall them within two hours.\nThis one in particular starts badly, with all the instructions given for mobile phones - tap here to start, tap the arrows to select the emoji you want to control and so on.. so, a full mobile port.\nThe store sells you just some different emoticons - the usual ones, the smile, the angry face, the sad one and so on; you can unlock them by collecting stars in-game, although they're both useless and basically unrecognizable apart from the smile on their yellow face and little else.\nIn fact, the game (as it often happens with these crappy mobile ports) is called \"Emoji Sliding Down\" when you open and play it, and only on Steam it has another title.\nMoreover, it's very user unfriendly - it's nice probably to kill some time on the mobile phone, but it sucks if you wanna play it on the PC. You're forced to hit enter to restart and at the same time you're forced to use the mouse to navigate through the menus (assuming you don't have a touch screen, I'm playing on a standard HP gaming laptop).. and you're not even given a tutorial.\nWhat you'll have to do is basically to control the clouds that act like platforms - starting top-down, your emoticon will sit on a cloud and with W and D you'll tilt all the clouds at once; the smile, being always (even if you change skins etc.) a yellow ball, will fall down them and you'll have to direct it by changing the clouds' direction.\nAs I said above, the whole game flows in a stupid way for what concerns physics and controls - the smile will often fall down the clouds just because it gets too fast and you can't control it properly, and the WD keys (or the directional ones, but you can't remap anything) sometimes aren't responsive so that you won't be able to tilt in time the clouds and you'll die.\nIt's extremely frustrating, since you'll see just 4-5 layers of clouds at a time and falling down, the clouds will appear randomly along with the red dots to collect and the coins, so that you can't even foresee your next moves.. and everything goes too fast, by the way.\nPlus, I've got to add another extremely negative feature - there's, as it often happens with these shovelware games, only an endless level. \nYes - you push, touch or whatever the start keys and you'll be up there on the first cloud, and everything will start upon clicking W or D. \nGoing down will net you stars used to unlock the other skins (and thus the few achievements this game has), while collecting the red dots will add up to your score - both counters are on the upper side of the screen.\nGiven the poor controls, the shallow features of the lone endless level, the crappy graphics, the unusefulness of the few skins you can unlock, this game is only plain frustrating.\nYou'll find yourself going down that wall of clouds, dying after 5-6 platforms and restart.. the scoreboard is totally pointless, the only things that's in some way important is the money counter since it helps you to unlock skins and achievements.\nOne can't really pay for such games. You'll just get bored and frustrated after five minutes, no matter what kind of gamer you are.",
